    "question": {
      ":question/id": "50dafbc4-d5a4-5ed6-b128-23b199d28c1f",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/f5/f5ba5f7cc2ea5aaf405db1abff7e6f28ed4378ba6a5ec88d73c6861ede1d75de.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(2)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph of $f(x)$ breaks at $x=2$,  it's impossible to draw the graph without taking our pencil off of the paper.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "31d407ae-a2b9-5e30-b1a3-54cedef852a4",
